## Test Anti-Pattern Audit — Severity-Ranked Findings

This test suite is a textbook example of **"coverage without verification"** — every production method is called (achieving line coverage), but almost nothing is actually asserted.

---

### 🔴 Critical — Tests That Prove Nothing

| # | Test | Anti-Pattern | What It Misses |
|---|------|-------------|----------------|
| 1 | `AddProduct_Works` (L17) | **Fire-and-forget** — no assertion at all | Could silently fail to persist; `Save` could be a no-op |
| 2 | `UpdatePrice_Works` (L33) | **Fire-and-forget** — no assertion | Price could remain unchanged (core business logic untested) |
| 3 | `RemoveProduct_Works` (L39) | **Fire-and-forget** — no assertion | Product could still exist after removal |
| 4 | `GetProductCount_Works` (L64) | **Fire-and-forget** — result captured but never checked | Count could be wrong; tested on empty store anyway |
| 5 | `ApplyBulkDiscount_Works` (L69) | **Fire-and-forget** — no assertion | Discount math (the most bug-prone logic) completely unverified |
| 6 | `ImportFromCsv_Works` (L85) | **Fire-and-forget** — no assertion | Parsing could corrupt data, wrong field mapping undetected |

### 🟠 High — Weak Assertions (Assert-Not-Null Only)

| # | Test | Problem |
|---|------|---------|
| 7 | `GetProduct_Works` (L26) | `Assert.IsNotNull` passes for *any* product — doesn't verify SKU, name, or price match |
| 8 | `SearchProducts_Works` (L48) | Asserts list is not null but doesn't check count or content — a search returning 0 results passes |
| 9 | `ExportToCsv_Works` (L77) | Asserts CSV string is not null — empty string passes, malformed output passes |
| 10 | `GetAllProducts_Works` (L56) | Same as above — empty list is not null |

### 🟡 Medium — Missing Negative/Edge-Case Tests

| # | Missing Scenario | Risk |
|---|-----------------|------|
| 11 | `UpdatePrice` with non-existent SKU | `KeyNotFoundException` path never exercised |
| 12 | `GetProduct` for missing SKU | Null-return path never verified |
| 13 | `ApplyBulkDiscount` with 0 or 1.0 fraction | Boundary math bugs (free items, negative prices) |
| 14 | `ImportFromCsv` with malformed input | No test for missing fields, bad decimals, empty lines |

---

### Concrete Fixes

```csharp
// 1. AddProduct — verify round-trip
[TestMethod]
public void AddProduct_PersistsProduct()
{
    var product = new Product("SKU-001", "Widget", 9.99m);
    _catalog.AddProduct(product);
    var retrieved = _catalog.GetProduct("SKU-001");
    Assert.AreEqual(product, retrieved);
}

// 2. UpdatePrice — verify the new price sticks
[TestMethod]
